review_comments:
> The semaphore is only to regain ownership of the work item and not of the whole queue right?

Correct

> Because the callback lives in the queue it is still in the ownership of the queue. If the semaphore is used (and in that case the done_handler must not be used) the done handler is still null and does not get called.

Well, so far the callback isn't in the mainline yet and so it has no users. So, yes, it's perfectly safe to assume, that nobody uses both so far. But I'd prefer to also make that clear in the code, that nobody should do that - for as long as we have both in place. How about
```
				if (queue->done_handler) {
					k_spin_unlock(&queue->lock, k);
					queue->done_handler(w);
					k_spin_unlock(&queue->lock, k);
				} else {
					k_sem_give(&w->done_sem);
				}
```
and - btw - yes, no need to drop the spinlock if the callback isn't used. Let me give this a -1 - I think this deserves at least a short discussion, and sorry if you do end up making a new revision and temporarily losing all the approvals.
